# Unity UI Toolkit and Asset Rules

For Phase 8B quiz UI, use UI Toolkit.

Use UXML for structure, USS for presentation, and C# presenters/controllers for behavior.

Use existing UI asset components first. Inspect existing UXML, USS, sprites, icons, fonts, UI references, panel backgrounds, style variables, prefabs, and project-owned variants before creating anything new.

Do not destructively edit vendor or third-party assets. Create project-owned variants, wrappers, prefabs, templates, or USS files.

Do not rebuild valid completed application scene UI only because the quiz phase uses UI Toolkit.

Keep application-scene UI hybrid if it already uses Canvas. Phase 8B quiz UI can be UI Toolkit.

Use clear backgrounds behind static UI. Avoid visually confusing backgrounds behind quiz questions, choices, buttons, and feedback.

Use readable typography, large tap targets, safe contrast, and child-friendly spacing.

Support Android landscape and safe area.

Use ListView or equivalent virtualized list behavior for potentially long quiz lists.

Cache VisualElement queries during initialization. Do not query the full tree repeatedly during updates.

Register and unregister callbacks safely.

If a screen uses both Canvas and UI Toolkit, document which layer owns input, focus, navigation, and blocking overlays.

Do not put provider calls directly into UXML-bound view scripts. Views should call presenters/services.

Quiz UI states must include loading, empty, locked, error/retry, active, submitting, and result states where relevant.
